# Security policy

## Reporting a vulnerability

Please report security issues privately{% if author_name %} to {{ author_name }}{% endif %} — do **not** open a public
issue for a vulnerability. {% if git_host == "github" %}Use [GitHub private vulnerability reporting](https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/security-advisories/guidance-on-reporting-and-writing-information-about-vulnerabilities/privately-reporting-a-security-vulnerability)
where available, or contact the maintainers directly.{% else %}Contact the maintainers directly.{% endif %}

Include: a description, reproduction steps, and the potential impact. We aim to acknowledge
reports promptly and will coordinate a fix and disclosure timeline with you.

## Scope

- Do not run intrusive tests against production systems.
- Never include real secrets in reports, issues, or pull requests.

## Supported versions

Security fixes target the latest released version on the default branch.
